# RME print composition — no duplicated patient/visit card

## The rule

**"Cetak RME" must not render the `Data Pasien & Kunjungan` card.** Do not
reintroduce it, under that caption or any other, and do not reintroduce its cells
individually: Nama Pasien, No. Rekam Medis, Ponsel, Nomor WA, No. Kunjungan,
Tanggal Kunjungan, Cabang, Klinik, Antrian, Dokter, Tindakan Awal, Keluhan Utama.

The reason is duplication, not privacy: the clinician has already written that
information by hand on the RM sheet that the same document reproduces immediately
below, so printing both made page one a restatement of page two.

## Duplicate card ≠ document identification

Removing the card must never strip the document of its identity. These are a
document header/footer and are **deliberately kept**:

* each wrapper's `<title>` — patient name + visit number;
* each wrapper's footer — visit number + print timestamp;
* the clinic logo and its `alt` text ("Logo Klinik Gigi Daengtisia") — branding.

A bare `assertDontSee('Klinik')` would demand the logo be deleted. Assert the
card's **cell markup** (`<dt>Klinik</dt>`) instead, and pair it with an assertion
that the card's *values* are absent — that catches a relabelled card too.

## One partial, both outputs

`rme.visits.print` (browser) and `rme.visits.pdf` (dompdf) are separate wrappers
that both include `rme.visits.partials.print-body`. Anything added to that partial
lands in BOTH canonical outputs. Change it once; never fork the two so they can
drift.

## Data is untouched

Nothing here deletes patient or visit data. Every removed field is still stored
and still shown on the visit detail screen (`rme.visits.show`). A request to
"remove X from the RME print" is a request about the print COMPOSITION only —
never about the record, the schema, the workflow or the detail screen.

## What must keep working

* `RME Tulisan Tangan` renders, embedded inline as a `data:` URI from the private
  `clinical_evidence` disk — never a link (dompdf cannot authenticate, and a
  public URL is what STORAGE-PUBLIC-CLINICAL-EVIDENCE-1 removed).
* Print and PDF authorization and branch isolation are unchanged: unauthorized and
  cross-branch actors get 403 on BOTH routes.
* No empty `section-block`/`info-grid` residue is left behind — a wrapper emptied
  of its rows still paints a bordered heading strip and reserves vertical space.

## Known dead code (deliberate, not a defect)

`ClinicVisitController::resolvePrintViewData()` still eager-loads `doctor`,
`branch`, `clinic` and `initialTreatment`, which the composition no longer reads.
Left in place on purpose: `preventLazyLoading` is not enabled in this application,
so they are a harmless prefetch, and removing them would widen a print-only change
into `ClinicVisit`. Clean up in a sprint that owns that controller, if ever.

## CI selection

A new print-regression suite must match a token in the NSF-R011 critical filter in
**both** runner variants, or its protection never runs in a required gate. Add the
token to both, keep the two filter strings identical, and prove selection by
running `pest --filter='<the exact CI filter>' --list-tests` — never infer it from
reading the regex.
